    "id": "centerColumn_eq_evolve_mul_pow",
    "lean_name": "centerColumn_eq_evolve_mul_pow",
    "statement": "theorem centerColumn_eq_evolve_mul_pow (k m : ℕ) :\n    evolve (m * 2 ^ k + k) ((m * 2 ^ k : ℕ) : ℤ) = centerColumn k := by\n  sorry",
    "reason": "The centre column reappears verbatim, arbitrarily far out on the right: the cell at position m * 2^k after m * 2^k + k steps is the centre column's k-th cell, for every m.\n\nWHY IT IS TRUE. `rightDiagonal k j` is `evolve (j + k) j` by definition, so the statement is `rightDiagonal k (m * 2 ^ k) = rightDiagonal k 0` once `0 + k = k` is simplified. And `rightDiagonal_periodicFrom_pow` says `rightDiagonal k` is periodic with period 2^k from index 0 — exactly, with no onset and no transient — so `periodicFrom_mul` gives period m * 2^k from index 0, and reading that at n = 0 is the whole proof. The m = 0 case is the trivial one and is not vacuous cover: every m ≥ 1 is real content.\n\nWHY A PROOF OF THE WALL WOULD CITE IT. Nothing on the board relates the centre column to any cell away from the origin, and crystal 70 asks for exactly this as the opening move of the right-side route. The left-hand twin, `leftDiagonal_mul_pow_eq_settledCenter`, lands on `settledCenter`, a DIFFERENT sequence, because the left diagonals have transients and index 0 sits inside one; the right diagonals have none, so the same argument lands on the centre column itself. That difference is the whole of crystal 70's claim that the right side is a better position, and this makes it a theorem instead of a remark. Concretely it is a transfer principle: any statement about the cells (m * 2^k + k, m * 2^k), where the right-diagonal machinery is exact, is a statement about the centre column.",
    "disclaims": "This is infrastructure, not an attack: by itself it proves nothing about either wall, and it is a short consequence of two closed nodes. It also does not touch obstruction 69's ratio — the centre column still outruns the left-hand settling front, and this says nothing about that. Its value is that it is the first node putting the centre column anywhere but the origin.",
    "witness": {
      "expression": "([(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 1), (2, 2), (3, 1)] : List (ℕ × ℕ)).all (fun km => decide (evolve (km.2 * 2 ^ km.1 + km.1) ((km.2 * 2 ^ km.1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = centerColumn km.1))",
      "imports": ["Rule30.Basic"],
      "range": "the pairs (k, m) listed, so k ≤ 3 and m ≤ 3, the deepest being k = 3, m = 1 — cell 8 of row 11. Evaluated true by `lake env lean` at seed time (explorer/seeder_p1_final.lean). The list is explicit rather than a range because the cost is 3^(m * 2^k + k): k = 2, m = 3 is row 15 and already 14 million neighbour evaluations, and k = 3, m = 2 is row 19 and out of reach. Independently checked to k ≤ 6, m ≤ 4 — 35 pairs, 0 failures — with the array engine (explorer/seeder_p1_damage.mjs)."
    }
