    "statement": "theorem centerColumn_density_tendsto_half_iff_excess_nat :\n    Filter.Tendsto centerColumnDensity Filter.atTop (nhds (1 / 2 : ℝ)) ↔\n      ∀ d : ℕ, 0 < d → ∃ N₀ : ℕ, ∀ N ≥ N₀,\n        2 * d * ((Finset.range N).filter fun n => centerColumn n = true).card ≤ d * N + N ∧\n          d * N ≤ 2 * d * ((Finset.range N).filter fun n => centerColumn n = true).card + N := by\n  sorry",
    "reason": "The board already has one bridge from the balance prize to arithmetic, centerColumn_density_tendsto_half_iff_excess, but it lands in ℝ with an absolute value over casts and a real ε. The captain's own rule says to state it in ℕ, and the record says why: two of the three budget exhaustions on 2026-09-07 were provers cycling on casts, and the two P2 nodes that were stated with |·| over casts (centerColumnCount_sandwich, centerColumn_excess_interpolate) each cost a ladder rung for a two-line fact. This is the same bridge with no reals and no absolute value anywhere: d is the reciprocal of ε, and the two ℕ inequalities are exactly |2 * count N - N| ≤ N / d multiplied through by d. Why a proof of centerColumn_density_tendsto_half would cite it: it is the last step. Every structural fact anyone could prove about the centre column is a fact about a natural-number count, so a proof arrives holding the right-hand side and needs this iff read right to left; and every intermediate P2 node after this one can be stated and proved entirely in ℕ, which is what iff_excess was landed to make possible and did not quite achieve.",
    "disclaims": "Proves nothing about rule 30 — it is true of any Bool sequence in the centre column's place, and it is a restatement of the prize, not a step towards it. No finite witness is possible: both sides quantify over all large N.",
    "route": {
      "tactics": "  have main : ∀ c N d : ℕ, 0 < d →\n      ((2 * d * c ≤ d * N + N ∧ d * N ≤ 2 * d * c + N) ↔\n        |2 * (c : ℝ) - (N : ℝ)| ≤ (1 / (d : ℝ)) * (N : ℝ)) := by\n    intro c N d hd\n    have hd' : (0 : ℝ) < d := by exact_mod_cast hd\n    have cancel : (d : ℝ) * (1 / (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ)) = (N : ℝ) := by field_simp\n    rw [abs_le]\n    constructor\n    · rintro ⟨k1, k2⟩\n      have k1' : 2 * (d : ℝ) * (c : ℝ) ≤ (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) + (N : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast k1\n      have k2' : (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) ≤ 2 * (d : ℝ) * (c : ℝ) + (N : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast k2\n      constructor\n      · have t : (d : ℝ) * ((N : ℝ) - 2 * (c : ℝ)) ≤ (d : ℝ) * (1 / (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ)) := by\n          rw [cancel]; nlinarith\n        have := le_of_mul_le_mul_left t hd'\n        linarith\n      · have t : (d : ℝ) * (2 * (c : ℝ) - (N : ℝ)) ≤ (d : ℝ) * (1 / (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ)) := by\n          rw [cancel]; nlinarith\n        have := le_of_mul_le_mul_left t hd'\n        linarith\n    · rintro ⟨k1, k2⟩\n      constructor\n      · have t := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left k2 hd'.le\n        rw [cancel] at t\n        have : 2 * (d : ℝ) * (c : ℝ) ≤ (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) + (N : ℝ) := by nlinarith\n        exact_mod_cast this\n      · have k1' : -(2 * (c : ℝ) - (N : ℝ)) ≤ 1 / (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) := by linarith\n        have t := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left k1' hd'.le\n        rw [cancel] at t\n        have : (d : ℝ) * (N : ℝ) ≤ 2 * (d : ℝ) * (c : ℝ) + (N : ℝ) := by nlinarith\n        exact_mod_cast this\n  rw [centerColumn_density_tendsto_half_iff_excess]\n  constructor\n  · intro h d hd\n    have hd' : (0 : ℝ) < d := by exact_mod_cast hd\n    obtain ⟨N₀, hN₀⟩ := h (1 / (d : ℝ)) (by positivity)\n    exact ⟨N₀, fun N hN => (main _ N d hd).mpr (hN₀ N hN)⟩\n  · intro h ε hε\n    obtain ⟨d, hdgt⟩ := exists_nat_gt (1 / ε)\n    have hpos : (0 : ℝ) < (d : ℝ) := lt_trans (by positivity) hdgt\n    have hdpos : 0 < d := by exact_mod_cast hpos\n    obtain ⟨N₀, hN₀⟩ := h d hdpos\n    refine ⟨N₀, fun N hN => ?_⟩\n    have hb := (main _ N d hdpos).mp (hN₀ N hN)\n    have hinv : 1 / (d : ℝ) ≤ ε := by\n      rw [div_le_iff₀ hpos]\n      rw [div_lt_iff₀ hε] at hdgt\n      nlinarith\n    have hN0 : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (N : ℝ) := Nat.cast_nonneg N\n    calc |2 * (((Finset.range N).filter fun n => centerColumn n = true).card : ℝ) - (N : ℝ)|\n        ≤ (1 / (d : ℝ)) * (N : ℝ) := hb\n      _ ≤ ε * (N : ℝ) := by nlinarith",
      "imports": ["Rule30.Prize", "Rule30.Proofs.CenterColumnDensityTendstoHalfIffExcess", "Mathlib.Tactic"]
    }
